      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm having some trouble with an iam policy. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to a specific s3 bucket but i keep getting an access denied error. i thought i had the permissions right but it's still failing. can u take a look at this json and see what i'm missing?\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your IAM policy seems to only allow the `s3:PutObject` action for the specified bucket. To list resources and read/write logs, you'll also need to include `s3:PutObject`, `s3:PutObjectTagging`, `s3:GetBucketLogging` and possibly others, depending on the SDK your Lambda uses. Check the AWS documentation for the exact permissions needed for Lambda logging. Here's an example that includes some additional permissions:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:PutObjectTagging\",\n        \"s3:GetBucketLogging\",\n        \"s3:ListBucket\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": [\n        \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket\",\n        \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-logs-bucket/*\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "source": "target",
